# Without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile's build stage pulls in
# the host machine's own node_modules (built for the host's OS/arch) and
# overwrites the node_modules the deps stage just installed *inside* the
# container — silently breaking reproducibility and defeating the whole
# point of a multi-stage build. Confirmed live: this caused "Cannot find
# package 'next'" at container startup because the host's top-level
# node_modules only has 3 hoisted packages (most of the tree lives under
# apps/web/node_modules on this machine's particular hoisting layout).
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next

# Never send secrets/private data into the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
certs/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

.git
.gitignore
Unifi API Specs/
docs/
